  "value": {
    "id": "FR-SVL-006",
    "title": "Servlet stop and release: refuse new requests, wait for in-flight exchanges to the deadline, then cut the rest",
    "type": "functional",
    "target": "wave-8",
    "status": "verified",
    "scope": "SVL",
    "filePath": "docs/spec/14.servlet-adapter.srs.md",
    "headingLine": 758,
    "metadata": {
      "Type": "functional",
      "Target": "wave-8",
      "Status": "verified",
      "Priority": "high",
      "Tags": "wave-8, feasibility:high, servlet, shutdown",
      "Risk": "high",
      "Stability": "evolving",
      "Verification Method": "test",
      "GitHub Issue": "https://github.com/Snoworca/NaruServe/issues/19",
      "Related Docs": "-"
    },
    "acceptanceCriteria": [
      {
        "id": "AC-1",
        "text": "With one slow plain request in flight, `stop(2, SECONDS)` makes a new request answer `503` with `Connection: close` and the standard error body at once, returns as soon as the slow request finishes (before the deadline), and a request that outlasts the deadline does not make `stop` return later than the deadline plus 1 s. [D-359; r3 W2-003]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 783
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-2",
        "text": "With open SSE streams, `shutdown` delivers the closing notice of FR-SSE-005 through the core, each stream's client sees the end of the chunked body within the shutdown timeout plus the D-344 margin, the `AsyncContext` of each stream is completed, and the executor is shut down. [D-359; FR-SSE-005]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 784
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-3",
        "text": "A stream whose client stopped reading is cut at the deadline: `stop` returns within the deadline plus 1 s and the stream's `AsyncContext` is completed, so the container closes the output (Jetty frees a blocked writer at once, another container at its own write timeout, which the test does not wait for); the deviation sentence is present in `docs/api/servlet.md` and `docs/api/sse.md` gains a pointer to it. [r5 W2-001]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 785
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-4",
        "text": "`release()` detaches the handler (later requests are answered `503`), `stop` and `release` are idempotent, `stop` before `bind` is harmless, and after `shutdown` returns a test finds no thread named `naruserve-servlet-sse-*` alive within 2 s and no upload temporary file of the app. [D-107; I-015]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 786
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-5",
        "text": "Every test of the module that starts the container asserts after shutdown that no server thread and no temporary upload file of that app remains (a shared test rule). [I-015]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 787
      }
    ],
